<section class="dispatch-grid" aria-label="Why Instar">
  <article class="dispatch dispatch--orange">
    <p class="dispatch-label">01 / WHY INSTAR</p>
    <h2>Idle means idle.</h2>
    <p>
      A suspended guest costs no periodic polls. The host wakes it for an event; independent async
      operations still make progress.
    </p>
    <a href="/docs/concepts/runtime-model">Open runtime notes ▸</a>
  </article>

  <article class="dispatch dispatch--blue">
    <p class="dispatch-label">02 / NATIVE BY DEFAULT</p>
    <h2>The window is not in Wasm.</h2>
    <p>
      Winit, layout, hit-testing, AccessKit, text shaping, CPU rendering, and presentation stay
      native and host-owned.
    </p>
    <a href="/docs/concepts/host-owned-ui">See the ownership split ▸</a>
  </article>

  <article class="dispatch dispatch--yellow">
    <p class="dispatch-label">03 / SMALL SURFACE</p>
    <h2>One command on purpose.</h2>
    <p>
      <code>instar run &lt;component.wasm&gt;</code> is the entire CLI. Project formats and packaging
      conventions remain deliberately unclaimed.
    </p>
    <a href="/docs/reference/cli">Read the CLI reference ▸</a>
  </article>
</section>
